Z||000003||Old Lar||12-14-2001||10:16 PM||||Try the FIERO PARTS VENDORS list top of page.  Click on it to see a list of places that sell used parts. Twin Lakes Fiero, in Illinois, Fiero Factory in Alabama and Kick Hill Farms in Conneticut have many parts and I'm sure one of them will have a cooling tube at a reasonable price.  Also check out the Fiero web ring for those who are not on the list.||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||12-15-2001||05:09 AM||||I have one here - call me toll free at 866-343-7648 and we can arrange something..<P>Terry<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg">  <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||shelfran||12-15-2001||02:16 PM||||Go to a Plumbing store and buy a piece of pipe 1 1/4" in diameter. Take the old one out, lay it beside the new pipe, borrow a bender from a friend or take it to a plumber and have them bend it to match the old one. Mine has lasted for 6 years!! The guy charged me 5 bucks to bend it.<P>Frank Sheldon<BR>Ticonderoga, Ny....PS  The Fiero Store also has one in their end of the year flyer...Frank||||reg||1
